00:00:03.710 THIS CHANNEL ANSWERS PACKETS - the default since 2026-09-14. It used to need
00:00:03.711   --set-field-probe, a flag every caller passed and whose absence cost a launch;
00:00:03.711   --silent-channel is the way to turn answering off now, and it is only for
00:00:03.711   eliminating the channel as a variable.
00:00:03.711   This channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
00:00:03.711   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
00:00:03.711   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
00:00:03.711   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
00:00:03.711   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
00:00:03.711   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
00:00:03.711   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
00:00:03.711   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
00:00:03.711   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
